{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PjYwz79UUMqJaD9ckCdYVy","type":"tool_result","content":"95:\\textbf{Proposed pair.} The selector--imputer pair of Section~\\ref{sec:impl}, selected on the development partition as the best-scoring configuration. The sealed evaluation ran either this pair or its latent-skill extension (below); the two have identical development scores, the recorded hash of the evaluated source tree matches neither retained source copy, and the available evidence cannot say which ran. Statements about the ``evaluated pair'' therefore refer to this selector--imputer family. \\textbf{Variant under search.} A simpler pair: z-scored columns, EM Gaussian, covariance-trace greedy selection with a coverage weighting, and the ridge-regularised Gaussian conditional mean, with shrinkage, factor rank and ridge strength tuned by history cross-validation. A third pair adds a monotone-link latent-skill member to the stack and a latent A-optimal selector candidate. The proposed pair and the simpler pair differ in several components at once (transform, selector candidates, stack, clipping), so their comparison (Table~\\ref{tab:search}) is a comparison of configurations, not an ablation. \\textbf{Evaluator baselines.} (a) \\emph{Column mean}: predict each benchmark's history mean. (b) \\emph{Random-$k$ ridge}: five random $k$-subsets (seeded from the dataset, $k$ and draw index), ridge imputer fitted on a rank-5 SVD-completed history (40 completion iterations), ridge strength chosen by leave-one-out over four values; the mean $\\nrmse$ over draws is the baseline. (c) \\emph{Greedy-forward ridge}: forward selection (up to 20 benchmarks) minimising leave-one-out ridge error on the remaining benchmarks of the completed history, with the same ridge imputer. Both ridge baselines share their imputer, so they probe selection with the imputer fixed; the proposed pair changes both selector and imputer.\n172:During development, three configurations were scored on a separate MTEB partition (disjoint groups, 280 columns, 131 history and 32 held-out models) with two seeds and $k\\in\\{2,5,10,20\\}$. Table~\\ref{tab:search} keeps these numbers apart from the sealed ones; $\\nrmse$ values are not comparable across the two partitions.\n178:\\label{tab:search}\n# Paper validation feedback\n\n- generated_at: 2026-11-11T13:02:34.319960+00:00\n- paper_dir: `work/results/r03/claude/20261111_111139/paper`\n- ok: `False`\n\n## Hard errors\n- figure validation failed: figure_manifest.json failed schema validation: figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].path_png: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].n_panels: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].panels_per_row: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].categories_per_panel: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].series_per_panel: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].max_label_chars: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].font_sizes: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].uses_abbrev_labels: Field required; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].files: Extra inputs are not permitted; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].panel_count: Extra inputs are not permitted; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].panels: Extra inputs are not permitted; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), LegacyFigureManifestFigure].required: Extra inputs are not permitted; figures.0.function-after[validate_panel_lengths(), RichFig